$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 08/Experimental design

::EPI-W8-001::What distinguishes an experimental study from an observational study? {
=The investigator assigns or determines the intervention/exposure#Correct.
~The sample must be larger#Review intervention-assignment and counterfactual logic.
~The outcome must be binary#Review intervention-assignment and counterfactual logic.
~No comparison group is used#Review intervention-assignment and counterfactual logic.
}

$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 08/Randomisation

::EPI-W8-002::What is the main causal purpose of random assignment? {
=Reduce systematic differences in baseline causes of outcome between groups on average#Correct.
~Guarantee identical groups#Review intervention-assignment and counterfactual logic.
~Remove all measurement error#Review intervention-assignment and counterfactual logic.
~Ensure every participant adheres#Review intervention-assignment and counterfactual logic.
}

::EPI-W8-003::In trial scenario 1, eligible participants are assigned by a computer-generated random sequence. What feature is being used? {
=Random allocation#Correct.
~Matching#A random sequence determines intervention assignment.
~Convenience sampling#A random sequence determines intervention assignment.
~Case-control sampling#A random sequence determines intervention assignment.
}

