$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 08/Blinding and allocation

::EPI-W8-013::What does allocation concealment primarily prevent? {
=Predicting upcoming treatment assignment during enrolment#Correct.
~Loss to follow-up#Review intervention-assignment and counterfactual logic.
~Outcome incidence#Review intervention-assignment and counterfactual logic.
~Cluster correlation#Review intervention-assignment and counterfactual logic.
}

::EPI-W8-014::Why might blinded outcome assessment be useful when participants cannot be blinded to an intervention? {
=It can reduce differential outcome classification#Correct.
~It creates randomisation after the fact#Blinding can reduce measurement bias even when treatment awareness cannot be hidden.
~It eliminates non-adherence#Blinding can reduce measurement bias even when treatment awareness cannot be hidden.
~It makes clustering disappear#Blinding can reduce measurement bias even when treatment awareness cannot be hidden.
}

