$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 08/Efficacy effectiveness

::EPI-W8-024::Which term usually refers to performance under ideal controlled conditions? {
=Efficacy#Correct.
~Effectiveness#Review intervention-assignment and counterfactual logic.
~Prevalence#Review intervention-assignment and counterfactual logic.
~Specificity#Review intervention-assignment and counterfactual logic.
}

::EPI-W8-025::Which term usually refers to performance under routine field conditions? {
=Effectiveness#Correct.
~Efficacy#Review intervention-assignment and counterfactual logic.
~Incidence#Review intervention-assignment and counterfactual logic.
~Odds#Review intervention-assignment and counterfactual logic.
}

$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 08/Cluster trials

::EPI-W8-026::A programme is assigned to whole health facilities rather than individual patients in scenario 1. What design issue must the analysis recognise? {
=Patients within the same facility may have correlated outcomes#Correct.
~Every patient is statistically independent by definition#Cluster randomisation creates within-cluster correlation.
~The study becomes case-control#Cluster randomisation creates within-cluster correlation.
~No control group is possible#Cluster randomisation creates within-cluster correlation.
}

::EPI-W8-027::A programme is assigned to whole health facilities rather than individual patients in scenario 2. What design issue must the analysis recognise? {
